Conversio: show windows when their native z-order sibling is hidden.

A quick Win32 minimize/restore clears WS_MINIMIZE before Cocoa finishes
miniaturizing the window. show_window() can therefore select a sibling which
Wine still considers on-screen but Cocoa reports as invisible. In orderBelow:
orAbove:activate:, prev is non-nil, next is nil, and the selected "other" becomes
nil. getSiblingWindowsForWindow: then throws while building arrayWithObject:nil,
leaving the new MessageBox unordered and interrupting main-thread requests.
A hidden next sibling is also unsuitable as an ordering target.

Only enter the relative-ordering path when at least one sibling is visible.
Otherwise use the existing order-front path, including parent ordering and
window-level adjustment. Visible sibling ordering is unchanged. Reproduced with
a standalone MinGW MessageBox test on revision 4, without Steam or D3DMetal.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -1753,7 +1753,11 @@
             if ([self becameEligibleParentOrChild])
                 needAdjustWindowLevels = TRUE;
 
-            if (prev || next)
+            /* Wine's z-order can still include a window Cocoa has miniaturized or
+               ordered out.  Only use a visible sibling; otherwise order to the
+               front below, rather than passing nil to getSiblingWindowsForWindow:
+               or ordering relative to a hidden window number. */
+            if ([prev isVisible] || [next isVisible])
             {
                 WineWindow* other = [prev isVisible] ? prev : next;
                 NSWindowOrderingMode orderingMode = [prev isVisible] ? NSWindowBelow : NSWindowAbove;
